# Shell scripts must keep LF endings even when checked out on Windows.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` is common on Windows checkouts and would rewrite these
# to CRLF. Alpine's `sh` then fails with a cryptic "no such file or directory"
# pointing at the interpreter line — a deploy failure that reads as a missing
# file rather than a line-ending problem, which is a bad hour to spend.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The container reads these directly; same reasoning.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
